.if \n[.g] .mso www.tmac
.TH SDL_AssertionHandler 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_AssertionHandler \- A callback that fires when an SDL assertion fails.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_assert.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef SDL_AssertState (SDLCALL *SDL_AssertionHandler)( const SDL_AssertData *data, void *userdata);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I data
a pointer to the
.BR SDL_AssertData
structure corresponding to the current assertion\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
what was passed as
.BR userdata
to
.BR SDL_SetAssertionHandler ()\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an
.BR SDL_AssertState
value indicating how to handle the failure\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This callback may be called from any thread that triggers an assert at any time\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

